          {
            "id": "p26-q30-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Weight the chance of guessing correctly after each possible answer by the probability of that answer.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "After a truthful answer, the possible cards remain equally likely. If $m$ cards give a yes answer, the conditional chances of a correct guess are $\\frac{1}{m}$ after yes and $\\frac{1}{(52-m)}$ after no.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{correct guess})&=\\frac{m}{52}\\times\\frac{1}{m}+\\frac{52-m}{52}\\times\\frac{1}{52-m}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{correct guess})&=\\frac{1}{52}+\\frac{1}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{correct guess})&=\\frac{1}{26}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe three questions have $m=26$, $m=12$ and $m=1$, respectively. Thus all three give the same chance of guessing correctly.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
